    {
      "id": "Q3b_iii",
      "text": "A computer has an operating system (OS).\n\nThe OS handles interrupts.\n\nA processor is currently executing a program. The processor receives an interrupt.\n\nExplain how the processor manages the current program and the interrupt.",
      "command": "Explain",
      "objective": "AO1",
      "marks": 5,
      "visuals": [],
      "page": 7,
      "layout_type": "SimpleSingleBlock",
      "structure_data": {
        "line_count": 10
      },
      "topic": "4.1",
      "topic_name": "Types of Software and Interrupts",
      "answers": {
        "type": "text",
        "visuals": [],
        "scoring_rule": "Any five from:",
        "marking_points": [
          {
            "text": "Interrupt is given priority",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "…and placed in interrupt queue",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "Processor finishes current FE cycle for program",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "Processor checks interrupt priority queue // processor checks for higher priority interrupt than program/process",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "If lower priority processor runs next FDE cycle for program/process // if lower priority processor continues with program/process",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "(if higher priority) processor stores current process/registers on stack",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "Checks source of interrupt",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "… and calls the appropriate ISR",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "ISR handles/resolves interrupt",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "If there is another higher priority interrupt (than process) then repeat",
            "marks": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "… (otherwise) processor retrieves content of stack/registers/previous process (to continue with process from program)",
            "marks": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      "difficulty": "High",
      "bloom_level": "Understand",
      "cognitive_load": "Low"
